  expected:
  actual: '<div class="section-intro"><span class="eyebrow">Map workspace</span><h2>Layers and legend</h2><p>Only integrated scientific layers will appear as available map controls.</p></div><section aria-label="Elevation" data-scientific-category="Elevation"><h3>Elevation</h3><p class="supporting">Terrain height relative to the source vertical reference; posting does not establish effective resolution or absolute accuracy.</p><div class="data-product"><label class="check-row"><input type="checkbox" checked=""/>Elevation<span class="badge cyan">Observed</span></label><p class="supporting">Availability: available</p><label class="field-label" for="opacity-jezero-elevation">Elevation opacity <span class="mono">60%</span></label><input id="opacity-jezero-elevation" type="range" min="0" max="100" value="60"/><div class="legend-detail"><strong>Elevation (areoid m; legacy shaded tint, clipped -2620/-1770) (m)</strong><div><p><span aria-hidden="true" style="background-color:#4655ac;width:16px;height:12px"></span>-2620 and below (mission native min -2640.53 m; unshaded tint)</p></div><div><p><span aria-hidden="true" style="background-color:#5288b6;width:16px;height:12px"></span>-2486.1 (unshaded tint)</p></div><div><p><span aria-hidden="true" style="background-color:#82aca6;width:16px;height:12px"></span>-2326.9 (unshaded tint)</p></div><div><p><span aria-hidden="true" style="background-color:#c8be8a;width:16px;height:12px"></span>-2141.4 (unshaded tint)</p></div><div><p><span aria-hidden="true" style="background-color:#e6d4a8;width:16px;height:12px"></span>-1935.6 (unshaded tint)</p></div><div><p><span aria-hidden="true" style="background-color:#f8f0e0;width:16px;height:12px"></span>-1770 and above (mission native max -1639.89 m; unshaded tint)</p></div></div><p class="supporting">USGS Astrogeology Science Center · NASA/MRO HiRISE · Mars 2020 TRN DTM mosaic (DOI 10.5066/P9REJ9JN) · Display-grade shaded elevation (hypsometric tint x analytic hillshade, sun 315 deg az / 45 deg alt, derived by team/jezero/terrain/build_terrain.mjs from the audited 1 m DTM), NOT the native 1 m posts and NOT a route-safety, hazard or engineering product. Vertical datum: areoid-relative meters, verified against the PLACES traverse (median DTM-PLACES offset +0.025 m, abs P95 4.3 m, 30,445 matched points; team/jezero/terrain/audit_terrain.mjs - all checks pass). Documented caveats: the far-west Jezero_CR stereo component (USGS-documented uncompensated y-parallax) carries a small positive bias (~+3 m mean, abs P95 ~4.9 m in the traverse bins crossing it); the FGDC published value range is understated - sampled values to -1639.971 m are real western-rim terrain confirmed by rover ground truth (PLACES sol 1354: -1786.0 m at 18.4575 N, 77.2685 E, matched within ~5 m). Ramp saturates at -2620/-1770 m (p2-p98 of the coverage); the display shares the region display-transform caveats (planetocentric display latitude on Web Mercator, pending the PPPCS ellipsoid review).</p><p class="supporting">Coverage: USGS Mars 2020 TRN HiRISE DTM mosaic (JEZ_hirise_soc_006, 1 m/px, DOI 10.5066/P9REJ9JN) over the Jezero exploration area: derived shaded-elevation display tiles cover 77.2229-77.4931 E, 18.4020-18.5197 N (Web-Mercator XYZ, zooms 5-14, 193 RGBA tiles; tile ranges span the region extent, data only within the footprint). Pixels outside the DTM footprint - including the supported extent&#x27;s west margin, 77.1868-77.2229 E - are transparent (no terrain data there).</p><details><summary>Scientific processing and verification</summary><p class="supporting">Elevation describes terrain height relative to the stated vertical reference. It helps identify topographic differences but does not independently establish route safety.</p><dl class="metadata"><div><dt>Source verification</dt><dd>VERIFIED</dd></div><div><dt>Processing verification</dt><dd>UNVERIFIED</dd></div><div><dt>Independent registration</dt><dd>UNVERIFIED</dd></div><div><dt>Nominal source posting</dt><dd>1 m; not effective resolution</dd></div><div><dt>Valid-data mask</dt><dd>Native DEM nodata; legacy output alpha. Existing tiles include tile-range margins, not a hard mission clip.</dd></div></dl><p class="supporting">Preserved shaded tint has incorrect Earth gradient spacing and flat-ground illumination. Native numeric elevations unchanged. Vertical reference is supported by historical PLACES height agreement; this is not independent absolute horizontal control.</p></details><details><summary>Source and processing details</summary><a href="https://doi.org/10.5066/P9REJ9JN" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">USGS Mars 2020 Terrain Relative Navigation HiRISE DTM mosaic (1 m/px)</a><p class="supporting">Product verified via its DOI landing page, FGDC metadata XML and ISIS label before download; source index https://asc-pds-services.s3.us-west-2.amazonaws.com/mosaic/mars2020_trn/HiRISE/index.html.</p><p class="supporting">Four-layer audit: standalone hillshade uses team/jezero/terrain/build_hillshade.py from the numeric source, artificial azimuth 315 / elevation 45 degrees, native pixel centers and Mars ground spacing, strict nodata support. Source SHA256, exact extrema, native mask geometry and per-tile hashes are in team/jezero/terrain/hillshade_report.json. Native label longitude domain is 180; positive Jezero longitudes are unchanged in application 0-360 east convention.</p><p class="supporting">Uncompressed 32-bit float GeoTIFF, 21,400 x 21,488, 1 m/px, equirectangular (latTs0/lon0), planetocentric latitude, east-positive, D_Mars_2000_Sphere r=3,396,190 m; ISIS label UpperLeftCornerX/Y = 4577366.0/1106618.0 m; GDAL nodata tag -3.4028e+38; label footprint 77.2229-77.5840 E, 18.3068-18.6693 N (reproduced exactly by the GeoTIFF georeferencing tags).</p><p class="supporting">Audit (team/jezero/terrain/audit_terrain.mjs, report team/jezero/terrain/audit_report.json): structure, georeferencing, nodata and value-range checks pass; PLACES cross-check over 30,445 traverse points: median DTM-PLACES +0.025 m, RMS 1.6 m, abs P95 4.3 m - the areoid-relative vertical datum is verified empirically.</p><p class="supporting">FGDC published value range (-2659.8 to -1942.1 m) is understated: sampled values reach -1639.971 m in a contiguous western-rim band (lon 77.25-77.29 E). Confirmed real terrain by rover ground truth (PLACES sol 1354: -1786.0 m at 18.4575 N, 77.2685 E; DTM matched within ~5 m) - recorded as a documented metadata caveat, not a data defect.</p><p class="supporting">USGS documents uncompensated y-parallax in the Jezero_CR stereo components of this mosaic; the traverse bins crossing that area show a small positive bias (~+3 m mean, abs P95 ~4.9 m) consistent with the USGS quality warning.</p><p class="supporting">Display tiles /maps/jezero/terrain-tiles/{z}/{x}/{y}.png derived by team/jezero/terrain/build_terrain.mjs: 193 256 px Web-Mercator XYZ RGBA tiles, zooms 5-14, shaded hypsometric elevation (p2-p98 ramp -2620/-1770 m) x analytic hillshade (sun 315 deg az / 45 deg alt); bilinear sampling; nodata transparent; the large source raster stays in local storage (team/jezero/terrain/, gitignored) and is never committed.</p><p class="supporting">Public domain USGS release; cite the product authors via the DOI.</p><p class="supporting">Four-layer audit identified incorrect Earth-sized gradient spacing and flat-ground illumination in the legacy elevation tint; existing pixels retained with processing UNVERIFIED. Legacy slope/elevation sampling also omits half-post center correction. These display issues do not invalidate the source elevations; standalone hillshade does not reuse those calculations. Independent absolute horizontal registration remains UNVERIFIED; historical PLACES height agreement is not independent positional control.</p><p class="supporting">Display tiles are derived, resampled and hillshaded - not the native 1 m posts; not a route-safety or engineering product.</p><p class="supporting">The far-west CR stereo component retains a small (~3-5 m) vertical bias per USGS quality notes; values there are display-grade only.</p></details></div></section><section aria-label="Hillshade" data-scientific-category="Hillshade"><h3>Hillshade</h3><p class="supporting">Artificial illumination reveals terrain shape. Intensity is unitless and does not represent actual sunlight or terrain safety.</p><p class="supporting">No dataset available.</p></section><section aria-label="Slope" data-scientific-category="Slope"><h3>Slope</h3><p class="supporting">Local terrain gradient in degrees. Display classes are not astronaut safety thresholds or a traversability assessment.</p><p class="supporting">No dataset available.</p></section><section aria-label="Thermal" data-scientific-category="Thermal"><h3>Thermal</h3><p class="supporting">Qualitative infrared mosaic brightness. This display is not calibrated temperature or thermal inertia; observation context differs by source.</p><p class="supporting">No dataset available.</p></section><section aria-label="Basemaps"><h3>Basemaps</h3><p class="supporting">Optical context and mission imagery.</p><p class="supporting">No dataset available.</p></section><section aria-label="Map overlays"><h3>Map overlays</h3><p class="supporting">Recorded traverses and dataset coverage outlines; these do not establish waypoint eligibility.</p><p class="supporting">No dataset available.</p></section><h3>Interface preview</h3><p class="supporting">Demonstration controls below affect schematic artwork only.</p><label class="check-row"><input type="checkbox"/>Show schematic preview <span class="badge science">Scenario</span></label><button class="full">View scientific data register</button>'
