in/audit_report.json): structure, georeferencing, nodata and value-range checks pass; PLACES cross-check over 30,445 traverse points: median DTM-PLACES +0.025 m, RMS 1.6 m, abs P95 4.3 m - the areoid-relative vertical datum is verified empirically.</p><p class="supporting">FGDC published value range (-2659.8 to -1942.1 m) is understated: sampled values reach -1639.971 m in a contiguous western-rim band (lon 77.25-77.29 E). Confirmed real terrain by rover ground truth (PLACES sol 1354: -1786.0 m at 18.4575 N, 77.2685 E; DTM matched within ~5 m) - recorded as a documented metadata caveat, not a data defect.</p><p class="supporting">USGS documents uncompensated y-parallax in the Jezero_CR stereo components of this mosaic; the traverse bins crossing that area show a small positive bias (~+3 m mean, abs P95 ~4.9 m) consistent with the USGS quality warning.</p><p class="supporting">Display tiles /maps/jezero/terrain-tiles/{z}/{x}/{y}.png derived by team/jezero/terrain/build_terrain.mjs: 193 256 px Web-Mercator XYZ RGBA tiles, zooms 5-14, shaded hypsometric elevation (p2-p98 ramp -2620/-1770 m) x analytic hillshade (sun 315 deg az / 45 deg alt); bilinear sampling; nodata transparent; the large source raster stays in local storage (team/jezero/terrain/, gitignored) and is never committed.</p><p class="supporting">Public domain USGS release; cite the product authors via the DOI.</p><p class="supporting">Four-layer audit identified incorrect Earth-sized gradient spacing and flat-ground illumination in the legacy elevation tint; existing pixels retained with processing UNVERIFIED. Legacy slope/elevation sampling also omits half-post center correction. These display issues do not invalidate the source elevations; standalone hillshade does not reuse those calculations. Independent absolute horizontal registration remains UNVERIFIED; historical PLACES height agreement is not independent positional control.</p><p class="supporting">Display tiles are derived, resampled and hillshaded - not the native 1 m posts; not a route-safety or engineering product.</p><p class="supporting">The far-west CR stereo component retains a small (~3-5 m) vertical bias per USGS quality notes; values there are display-grade only.</p></details></div></section><section aria-label="Thermal" data-scientific-category="Thermal"><h3>Thermal</h3><p class="supporting">Qualitative infrared mosaic brightness. This display is not calibrated temperature or thermal inertia; observation context differs by source.</p><p class="supporting">No dataset available.</p></section><section aria-label="Basemaps"><h3>Basemaps</h3><p class="supporting">Optical context and mission imagery.</p><p class="supporting">No dataset available.</p></section><section aria-label="Map overlays"><h3>Map overlays</h3><p class="supporting">Recorded traverses and dataset coverage outlines; these do not establish waypoint eligibility.</p><p class="supporting">No dataset available.</p></section><h3>Interface preview</h3><p class="supporting">Demonstration controls below affect schematic artwork only.</p><label class="check-row"><input type="checkbox"/>Show schematic preview <span class="badge science">Scenario</span></label><button class="full">View scientific data register</button>'
