ss="supporting">ESA / DLR / Freie Universität Berlin / NASA / JPL-Caltech · Divya M. Persaud / Alfiah Diana Rizky Putri / Jan-Peter Muller (2021), DOI 10.5281/zenodo.5808354 · Marswalk DEM derivatives · 30 m nominal posting and 90 m north gradient support for derivatives; neither establishes effective resolution or absolute accuracy. Derived from HRSC stereo images H1938_0000, H1927_0000, and H1916_0000 tied to HRSC-MOLA 200 m global DTM. Heights in metres above MOLA areoid. Co-registration against CTX mosaic unverified; not for hazard routing or astronaut safety certification.</p><p class="supporting">Coverage: Regional crop from the broader HRSC source mosaic: 8.70 × 16.29 km, 141.733079 km². Fully valid crop covers 100% of the Gale overview and intentionally extends beyond the fixed optical overview. Outside crop transparent. CTX alignment unverified.</p><details class="product-metadata"><summary>Regional HRSC elevation data coverage and scale</summary><dl class="metadata"><div><dt>Original source product</dt><dd>hrsc_km09_h1938_h1927_h1916-dtm-mosaic.tif · DOI 10.5281/zenodo.5808354</dd></div><div><dt>Source coverage</dt><dd>Original HRSC mosaic: 135.890569–139.728969° E, −8.184239–−2.983875° N; valid source coverage is irregular.</dd></div><div><dt>Application display crop</dt><dd>Selected 291 × 543 grid, about 8.70 × 16.29 km (141.733079 km²). Intentionally extends about 1 km beyond the fixed 96.259148 km² optical overview. Mission View bounds restrict default display to mission footprint.</dd></div><div><dt>Valid-data coverage</dt><dd>All 158,013 derived cells valid; fully valid rectangular crop covering 100% of the Gale overview. Outside this crop is unavailable and transparent.</dd></div><div><dt>Nominal posting</dt><dd>30 m; spacing of elevation samples, not measured effective resolution</dd></div><div><dt>North gradient support</dt><dd>90 m; neighborhood used for slope and hillshade, not absolute measurement accuracy</dd></div><div><dt>Coordinate reference system</dt><dd>Mars sphere R=3,396,190 m; equirectangular, standard parallel/central meridian 0; planetocentric latitude, east longitude. Heights relative to MOLA areoid. Source datum name is unspecified.</dd></div><div><dt>Scientific limitations</dt><dd>30 m nominal posting and 90 m north gradient support for derivatives; neither establishes effective resolution or absolute accuracy. Derived from HRSC stereo images H1938_0000, H1927_0000, and H1916_0000 tied to HRSC-MOLA 200 m global DTM. Heights in metres above MOLA areoid. Co-registration against CTX mosaic unverified; not for hazard routing or astronaut safety certification.</dd></div></dl></details><details><summary>Source and processing details</summary><a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.5808354" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">30-m HRSC DTM Mosaic of Gale Crater, Mars</a><p class="supporting">Processed from HRSC stereo image orbits H1938_0000, H1927_0000, and H1916_0000 using DLR-VICAR modification (Kim and Muller 2009; Persaud et al. 2021).</p><p class="supporting">Equidistant cylindrical projection on Mars 2000 sphere R=3396190 m, lat_ts=0, lon_0=0. Heights in metres relative to MOLA areoid via 200 m HRSC-MOLA blended DTM control.</p><p class="supporting">Horn 3x3 derivative filters with metric cos(latitude) scaling for slope and NW artificial hillshade (315° az, 45° alt).</p><p class="supporting">Valid data coverage: 100.00% across the entire Gale Overview footprint. Audited in team/gale/G4_TERRAIN_AUDIT.json.</p><p class="supporting">Published under CC BY 4.0: Divya M. Persaud, Alfiah Diana Rizky Putri and Jan-Peter Muller (2021), 30-m HRSC DTM Mosaic of Gale Crater, Mars, DOI: 10.5281/zenodo.5808354.</p><p class="supporting">Fine-scale pixel co-registration against CTX optical mosaic is unverified. Do not infer sub-pixel alignment.</p><p class="supporting">30 m nominal posting and 90 m north gradient support do not establish effective spatial resolution or absolute accuracy; small boulders, suit-scale obstacles, and localized hazards are unresolved. Not for astronaut hazard or safety routing.</p></details></div></section><section aria-label="Hillshade" data-scientific-category="Hillshade"><h3>Hillshade</h3><p class="supporting">Artificial illumination reveals terrain shape. Intensity is unitless and does not represent actual sunlight or terrain safety.</p><p class="supporting">No dataset available.</p></section><section aria-label="Slope" data-scientific-category="Slope"><h3>Slope</h3><p class="supporting">Local terrain gradient in degrees. Display classes are not astronaut safety thresholds or a traversability assessment.</p><p class="supporting">No dataset available.</p></section><section aria-label="Thermal" data-scientific-category="Thermal"><h3>Thermal</h3><p class="supporting">Qualitative infrared mosaic brightness. This display is not calibrated temperature or thermal inertia; observation context differs by source.</p><p class="supporting">No dataset available.</p></section><section aria-label="Basemaps"><h3>Basemaps</h3><p class="supporting">Optical context and mission imagery.</p><p class="supporting">No dataset available.</p></section><section aria-label="Map overlays"><h3>Map overlays</h3><p class="supporting">Recorded traverses and dataset coverage outlines; these do not establish waypoint eligibility.</p><p class="supporting">No dataset available.</p></section><h3>Interface preview</h3><p class="supporting">Demonstration controls below affect schematic artwork only.</p><label class="check-row"><input type="checkbox"/>Show schematic preview <span class="badge science">Scenario</span></label><button class="full">View scientific data register</button>'
