 unquantified. Local orthophoto/CTX comparison indicates a possible positional mismatch; no fitted shift applied. Full-opacity independent DEM view by default. Slope alone is not astronaut safety, hazards or routing evidence.</p><p class="supporting">Coverage: Audited 1 km projected square in the historical Curiosity corridor, 137.371118..137.387989 E, -4.737706..-4.720835 N. 1,600 valid analysis cells; outside is unaudited and transparent. Toggling preserves the current camera. CTX alignment is unverified locally: do not match fine features between these products.</p><details><summary>Source and processing details</summary><a href="https://planetarydata.jpl.nasa.gov/img/data/msl/msl_places/data_maps/msl_orbital_dem.xml" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">PDS PLACES v42.0 - bounded orbital DEM subset</a><p class="supporting">Native 1 m post spacing, not uniform effective resolution. Equirectangular Mars sphere R=3396190 m, lat_ts=0, lon_0=0; planetocentric latitude / east longitude. Big-endian float32 image; fractional DEM origin retained, not copied from the orthophoto grid.</p><p class="supporting">MOLA areoid heights, metres positive up (PLACES SIS section 3.9.3). No radius conversion, fitted bias or translation. Bounded 28.31 MB source row range; full raster not downloaded.</p><p class="supporting">25 x 25 complete-post means, then Horn 3 x 3 gradients (75 m support). East metre spacing corrected by cos(latitude). Slope in degrees; hillshade artificial azimuth315 degrees / altitude45 degrees. No exaggeration or cast shadows.</p><p class="supporting">All 1,102,500 input posts valid; derived support 40 x 40 cells, outside transparent. Reproduction: team/gale/prepare_g3_2_dem.py; hashes and gate decisions: team/gale/G3_2_DEM_AUDIT.json.</p><p class="supporting">Precise local alignment to CTX is NOT verified. Direct mission-orthophoto/CTX check suggests positional mismatch. Published coordinates retained; full-opacity independent views by default. Do not match fine features between products.</p><p class="supporting">Mixed HiRISE/CTX lineage without per-pixel resolving-power or error map. 25 m analysis grid and 75 m derivative support do not certify effective spatial resolution. Absolute elevation, horizontal and slope error unquantified.</p><p class="supporting">1 km projected square only, not whole Gale or all rover exploration. Archive release time span is not stereo acquisition time. No hazard, astronaut-safety, routing or resource conclusions.</p></details></div></section><section aria-label="Hillshade" data-scientific-category="Hillshade"><h3>Hillshade</h3><p class="supporting">Artificial illumination reveals terrain shape. Intensity is unitless and does not represent actual sunlight or terrain safety.</p><p class="supporting">No dataset available.</p></section><section aria-label="Slope" data-scientific-category="Slope"><h3>Slope</h3><p class="supporting">Local terrain gradient in degrees. Display classes are not astronaut safety thresholds or a traversability assessment.</p><p class="supporting">No dataset available.</p></section><section aria-label="Thermal" data-scientific-category="Thermal"><h3>Thermal</h3><p class="supporting">Qualitative infrared mosaic brightness. This display is not calibrated temperature or thermal inertia; observation context differs by source.</p><p class="supporting">No dataset available.</p></section><section aria-label="Basemaps"><h3>Basemaps</h3><p class="supporting">Optical context and mission imagery.</p><p class="supporting">No dataset available.</p></section><section aria-label="Map overlays"><h3>Map overlays</h3><p class="supporting">Recorded traverses and dataset coverage outlines; these do not establish waypoint eligibility.</p><p class="supporting">No dataset available.</p></section><h3>Interface preview</h3><p class="supporting">Demonstration controls below affect schematic artwork only.</p><label class="check-row"><input type="checkbox"/>Show schematic preview <span class="badge science">Scenario</span></label><button class="full">View scientific data register</button>'
