e</dt><dd>Original HRSC mosaic: 135.890569–139.728969° E, −8.184239–−2.983875° N; valid source coverage is irregular.</dd></div><div><dt>Application display crop</dt><dd>Selected 291 × 543 grid, about 8.70 × 16.29 km (141.733079 km²). Intentionally extends about 1 km beyond the fixed 96.259148 km² optical overview. Mission View bounds restrict default display to mission footprint.</dd></div><div><dt>Valid-data coverage</dt><dd>All 158,013 derived cells valid; fully valid rectangular crop covering 100% of the Gale overview. Outside this crop is unavailable and transparent.</dd></div><div><dt>Nominal posting</dt><dd>30 m; spacing of elevation samples, not measured effective resolution</dd></div><div><dt>North gradient support</dt><dd>90 m; neighborhood used for slope and hillshade, not absolute measurement accuracy</dd></div><div><dt>Coordinate reference system</dt><dd>Mars sphere R=3,396,190 m; equirectangular, standard parallel/central meridian 0; planetocentric latitude, east longitude. Heights relative to MOLA areoid. Source datum name is unspecified.</dd></div><div><dt>Scientific limitations</dt><dd>30 m nominal posting and 90 m north gradient support for derivatives; neither establishes effective resolution or absolute accuracy. Derived from HRSC stereo images H1938_0000, H1927_0000, and H1916_0000 tied to HRSC-MOLA 200 m global DTM. Heights in metres above MOLA areoid. Co-registration against CTX mosaic unverified; not for hazard routing or astronaut safety certification.</dd></div></dl></details><details><summary>Source and processing details</summary><a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.5808354" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">30-m HRSC DTM Mosaic of Gale Crater, Mars</a><p class="supporting">Processed from HRSC stereo image orbits H1938_0000, H1927_0000, and H1916_0000 using DLR-VICAR modification (Kim and Muller 2009; Persaud et al. 2021).</p><p class="supporting">Equidistant cylindrical projection on Mars 2000 sphere R=3396190 m, lat_ts=0, lon_0=0. Hei