th:16px;height:12px"></span>10 to &lt; 15°</p><p class="supporting">Moderate slope on broad 200 m baseline.</p></div><div><p><span aria-hidden="true" style="background-color:#C25E2E;width:16px;height:12px"></span>15 to &lt; 20°</p><p class="supporting">Steeper slope on broad 200 m baseline.</p></div><div><p><span aria-hidden="true" style="background-color:#8C382A;width:16px;height:12px"></span>20° and above</p><p class="supporting">Broad 200 m slope only; suit-scale hazards completely unresolved.</p></div></div><p class="supporting">USGS Astrogeology Science Center · NASA / ESA · Fergason et al. (2018) · Marswalk DEM derivatives · 200 m nominal posting blending Mars Express HRSC and MGS MOLA elevation observations. 600 m north gradient support for derivatives. Neither posting nor support establishes effective spatial resolution or absolute accuracy; absolute positional and slope uncertainty unmeasured. Coarse regional baseline; small rocks, boulders, and local rover/suit hazards are completely unresolved. Not for astronaut hazard or safety routing.</p><p class="supporting">Coverage: Original source is a global HRSC–MOLA product; Marswalk serves a localized Gale-area crop, about 35.28 × 47.20 km (1,665.252534 km²), not a complete Gale Crater map. All 41,772 derived cells valid; covers the fixed optical overview. Outside crop transparent. CTX/color alignment remains unverified.</p><details class="product-metadata"><summary>Global HRSC–MOLA slope · degrees data coverage and scale</summary><dl class="metadata"><div><dt>Original source product</dt><dd>Mars_HRSC_MOLA_BlendDEM_Global_200mp_v2.tif · Fergason et al. (2018)</dd></div><div><dt>Source coverage</dt><dd>Original product is near-global on a Mars spherical geographic grid. Complete global valid-data mask not inspected; local subset validity verified.</dd></div><div><dt>Application display crop</dt><dd>Localized Gale-area crop: 177 × 236 cells, about 35.28 × 47.20 km (1,665.252534 km²). Not a complete Gale Crater map. Mission View bounds restrict default display to mission footprint.</dd></div><div><dt>Valid-data coverage</dt><dd>All 41,772 derived cells valid; fully valid rectangular crop covering 100% of the fixed optical overview. Outside this crop is unavailable and transparent.</dd></div><div><dt>Nominal posting</dt><dd>200 m; spacing of elevation samples, not measured effective resolution</dd></div><div><dt>North gradient support</dt><dd>600 m; neighborhood used for slope and hillshade, not absolute measurement accuracy</dd></div><div><dt>Coordinate reference system</dt><dd>Mars 2000 sphere R=3,396,190 m; geographic grid, 0.003374120830641° posting, planetocentric latitude and east longitude. Heights relative to MOLA areoid.</dd></div><div><dt>Scientific limitations</dt><dd>200 m nominal posting blending Mars Express HRSC and MGS MOLA elevation observations. 600 m north gradient support for derivatives. Neither posting nor support establishes effective spatial resolution or absolute accuracy; absolute positional and slope uncertainty unmeasured. Coarse regional baseline; small rocks, boulders, and local rover/suit hazards are completely unresolved. Not for astronaut hazard or safety routing.</dd></div></dl></details><details><summary>Source and processing details</summary><a href="https://astrogeology.usgs.gov/search/map/mars_mgs_mola_mex_hrsc_blended_dem_global_200m" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">USGS HRSC and MOLA Blended DEM Global 200m v2</a><p class="supporting">Fergason, Hare, and Laura (2018), Astrogeology PDS Annex, U.S. Geological Survey.</p><p class="supporting">Global nominal 200 m blended digital elevation model. Geographic angular grid on Mars sphere R=3396190 m; source-specific affine preserved.</p><p class="supporting">Bounded extraction of a localized Gale-area crop, about 35.28 × 47.20 km; not a complete Gale Crater map. Original global source retained via HTTP range requests without downloading the full 11.4 GB raster.</p><p class="supporting">Horn 3x3 derivatives on nominal 200 m grid with 600 m north gradient support for slope in degrees and NW artificial illumination hillshade; neither scale establishes effective resolution or accuracy.</p><p class="supporting">Official USGS product cited: Fergason et al. (2018), HRSC and MOLA Blended Digital Elevation Model at 200m V2.</p><p class="supporting">Broad 200 m regional baseline; does not resolve spacesuit-scale terrain hazards, rocks, or rover obstacles.</p><p class="supporting">Co-registration to optical CTX mosaic is uncertified. Not for astronaut safety routing or hazard certification.</p></details></div></section><section aria-label="Thermal" data-scientific-category="Thermal"><h3>Thermal</h3><p class="supporting">Qualitative infrared mosaic brightness. This display is not calibrated temperature or thermal inertia; observation context differs by source.</p><p class="supporting">No dataset available.</p></section><section aria-label="Basemaps"><h3>Basemaps</h3><p class="supporting">Optical context and mission imagery.</p><p class="supporting">No dataset available.</p></section><section aria-label="Map overlays"><h3>Map overlays</h3><p class="supporting">Recorded traverses and dataset coverage outlines; these do not establish waypoint eligibility.</p><p class="supporting">No dataset available.</p></section><h3>Interface preview</h3><p class="supporting">Demonstration controls below affect schematic artwork only.</p><label class="check-row"><input type="checkbox"/>Show schematic preview <span class="badge science">Scenario</span></label><button class="full">View scientific data register</button>'
