  actual: '<div class="section-intro"><span class="eyebrow">Map workspace</span><h2>Layers and legend</h2><p>Only integrated scientific layers will appear as available map controls.</p></div><section aria-label="Elevation" data-scientific-category="Elevation"><h3>Elevation</h3><p class="supporting">Terrain height relative to the source vertical reference; posting does not establish effective resolution or absolute accuracy.</p><p class="supporting">No dataset available.</p></section><section aria-label="Hillshade" data-scientific-category="Hillshade"><h3>Hillshade</h3><p class="supporting">Artificial illumination reveals terrain shape. Intensity is unitless and does not represent actual sunlight or terrain safety.</p><p class="supporting">No dataset available.</p></section><section aria-label="Slope" data-scientific-category="Slope"><h3>Slope</h3><p class="supporting">Local terrain gradient in degrees. Display classes are not astronaut safety thresholds or a traversability assessment.</p><div class="data-product"><label class="check-row"><input type="checkbox" checked=""/>Regional slope (MOLA)<span class="badge cyan">Derived</span></label><p class="supporting">Availability: available</p><label class="field-label" for="opacity-oxia-slope">Regional slope (MOLA) opacity <span class="mono">60%</span></label><input id="opacity-oxia-slope" type="range" min="0" max="100" value="60"/><div class="legend-detail"><strong>Regional slope from MOLA (~463 m). Not a safety assessment. (degrees)</strong><div><p><span aria-hidden="true" style="background-color:#FFFFCC;width:16px;height:12px"></span>0-2</p></div><div><p><span aria-hidden="true" style="background-color:#FED976;width:16px;height:12px"></span>2-5</p></div><div><p><span aria-hidden="true" style="background-color:#FD8D3C;width:16px;height:12px"></span>5-10</p></div><div><p><span aria-hidden="true" style="background-color:#E31A1C;width:16px;height:12px"></span>10-20</p></div><div><p><span aria-hidden="true" style="background-color:#800026;width:16px;height:12px"></span>&gt;20 degrees: regional numerical slope class. MOLA (~463 m) does not resolve small steep features. Not an astronaut safety threshold.</p></div></div><p class="supporting">NASA MGS MOLA Global DEM · via NASA JPL Mars Trek elevation-profile service · Regional slope from MOLA (~463 m). Small banks, boulders and walking-scale hazards are not resolved. Not a safety assessment. MOLA only across the whole area: the sharper HRSC-derived detail seen in parts of the hillshade is not in this layer. Tiles end at zoom 9; closer zooms enlarge them. Slope from central differences on a 0.01 degree grid interpolated from MOLA, using Mars 2000 sphere distances (R = 3,396,190 m); steep short slopes are smoothed out, so real local slopes can exceed the mapped class. The &gt;20 degree class marks slopes beyond NASA&#x27;s 20 degree suited-walking figure: NASA EVA-EXP-0042 Rev B, Exploration EVA System Concept of Operations (Oct 19, 2020), p.38, &#x27;Walking up/down/across a slope of up to 20°&#x27; (source oxia-nasa-eva-exp-0042); NASA ICES-2025-129 (Kim et al., funded by the NASA Mars Campaign Office), p.7, treats slopes beyond +/-20 degrees as inaccessible no-go zones (source oxia-nasa-ices-2025-129). That figure is lunar-derived and Mars gravity is higher. In this area 56 of 41,205 cells (18.8 km2, 0.14%) exceed 20 degrees, mostly one patch near 17.21 N, 335.07 E.</p><p class="supporting">Coverage: Slope in degrees over the team-chosen Oxia display area, 17.11-19.15 N, 334.60-336.60 E, from a 201 x 205 elevation grid (0.01 degree, about 0.59 km) sampled from the Mars Trek elevation-profile service (MGS MOLA, Global DEM). 26 display tiles, zooms 5-9. Grid: /maps/oxia/elevation-grid.json.</p><details><summary>Source and processing details</summary><a href="https://trek.nasa.gov/mars/TrekServices/ws/elevationProfile/multiDEM/interpolated" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">NASA JPL Mars Trek elevation-profile service (multiDEM/interpolated), DEM &#x27;MGS MOLA, Global DEM&#x27;</a><p class="supporting">Mars Trek is listed in the Space Apps 2026 challenge resources; this is the service behind Mars Trek&#x27;s own Elevation Profile tool (https://trek.nasa.gov/mars/jpl/config/config.json, services.multiDEMService.equirect).</p><p class="supporting">Sampled 2026-11-14 by team/oxia/terrain/build_mola_slope.mjs: one request per latitude row (205 rows, 17.11-19.15 N), path [[-25.40,lat],[-23.40,lat]], numberOfPoints=201, radiusInMeters=3390000; points snapped to a 0.01 degree grid. 0 no-data samples (No_Data_Value -32768). Elevations -3791.46 to -2381.14 m.</p><p class="supporting">Grid saved as /maps/oxia/elevation-grid.json (201 x 205, 360 KB). Slope (degrees) from central differences with Mars 2000 sphere distances, R = 3,396,190 m: median 0.68, p95 4.29, max 27.94; see team/oxia/terrain/slope_report.json.</p><p class="supporting">The service sends no CORS header, so browsers cannot call it from this app&#x27;s origin; data is pre-baked.</p><p class="supporting">Real detail is MOLA (~463 m); 0.01 degree samples interpolate it and add no detail.</p><p class="supporting">Elevations are as returned by the service (MOLA heights relative to the Mars areoid); the service does not state its interpolation method.</p><p class="supporting">Not walking-scale terrain and not a safety or hazard assessment.</p></details></div></section><section aria-label="Thermal" data-scientific-category="Thermal"><h3>Thermal</h3><p class="supporting">Qualitative infrared mosaic brightness. This display is not calibrated temperature or thermal inertia; observation context differs by source.</p><p class="supporting">No dataset available.</p></section><section aria-label="Basemaps"><h3>Basemaps</h3><p class="supporting">Optical context and mission imagery.</p><p class="supporting">No dataset available.</p></section><section aria-label="Map overlays"><h3>Map overlays</h3><p class="supporting">Recorded traverses and dataset coverage outlines; these do not establish waypoint eligibility.</p><p class="supporting">No dataset available.</p></section><h3>Interface preview</h3><p class="supporting">Demonstration controls below affect schematic artwork only.</p><label class="check-row"><input type="checkbox"/>Show schematic preview <span class="badge science">Scenario</span></label><button class="full">View scientific data register</button>'
