ight, Global Mosaic&#x27; (THEMIS_NightIR_ControlledMosaics_100m_v2_oct2018)</a><p class="supporting">Mars Trek is listed in the Space Apps 2026 challenge resources.</p><p class="supporting">Mars Trek description: geodetically controlled THEMIS night-IR mosaic tied to USGS Viking MDIM 2.1, orthoprojected at 100 m/pixel; 2017 preliminary release with further adjustments in the 2018 release.</p><p class="supporting">WMTS (checked 2026-11-14): EPSG::104905 (Mars 2000 sphere), TopLeftCorner -180/90, 256 px gray+alpha PNG tiles, levels 0-9 (level 9 is the finest; level 10 returns 404).</p><p class="supporting">Display tiles /maps/oxia/themis-night-tiles/ built by team/oxia/thermal/prepare_themis_night.mjs (nearest-neighbour, source gray values unchanged and coloured for display with the matplotlib inferno ramp, source alpha kept); see team/oxia/thermal/build_report.json.</p><p class="supporting">Pixel values are relative 8-bit brightness, not calibrated temperature (Mars Trek states no units or calibration).</p><p class="supporting">Observation period not confirmed: Mars Trek FGDC metadata has placeholder dates (19700101) and status &#x27;In work&#x27;.</p></details></div></section><section aria-label="Basemaps"><h3>Basemaps</h3><p class="supporting">Optical context and mission imagery.</p><p class="supporting">No dataset available.</p></section><section aria-label="Map overlays"><h3>Map overlays</h3><p class="supporting">Recorded traverses and dataset coverage outlines; these do not establish waypoint eligibility.</p><p class="supporting">No dataset available.</p></section><h3>Interface preview</h3><p class="supporting">Demonstration controls below affect schematic artwork only.</p><label class="check-row"><input type="checkbox"/>Show schematic preview <span class="badge science">Scenario</span></label><button class="full">View scientific data register</button>'
